CON-19: divide the swale and pavement surface flux by the vegetation void fraction

The surface layer's water fills only the fraction 1 - VegFrac of the space
above the surface. LIDSolver::swaleFluxRates() and
LIDSolver::pavementFluxRates() book the stored surface volume with that
void fraction but advanced the surface depth with the net inflow rate
alone, so with VegFrac > 0 only part of the net inflow showed up as storage
and the rest was lost from the water balance (or created when the surface
drained). Divide the surface depth rate by the
void fraction, as biocellFluxRates(), trenchFluxRates() and the reference
manual's surface layer equation already do. Nothing changes when VegFrac = 0.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-19_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/LID.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/LID.cpp
index 9aa0c73..e7c7510 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydrology/LID.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydrology/LID.cpp
@@ -1082,7 +1082,8 @@ public:
             SurfaceInfil = std::min(SurfaceInfil, maxRate);
         }
         SurfaceOutflow = getSurfaceOutflowRate(surfaceDepth);
-        f[L_SURF] = SurfaceInflow - SurfaceEvap - SurfaceInfil - SurfaceOutflow;
+        f[L_SURF] = (SurfaceInflow - SurfaceEvap - SurfaceInfil - SurfaceOutflow) /
+                    P->surf_void;
         f[L_PAVE] = (SurfaceInfil - PaveEvap - PavePerc) / paveVoidFrac;
         if (P->soil_thick > 0.0) {
             f[L_SOIL] = (PavePerc - SoilEvap - SoilPerc) / soilThickness;
@@ -1140,7 +1141,7 @@ public:
         SurfaceEvap /= lidArea;
         StorageExfil /= lidArea;
         SurfaceOutflow /= lidArea;
-        f[L_SURF] = dVdT / surfArea;
+        f[L_SURF] = dVdT / (surfArea * P->surf_void);
         f[L_SOIL] = 0.0;
         f[L_STOR] = 0.0;
         SurfaceVolume = volume / lidArea;
